1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,620
Lord, I feel tired — and if you do too,
you're in the right place.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,780
Nothing here needs following; it's just
going to keep going.

3
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:19,460
The whole of Second Samuel, slowly: David,
Absalom, one long

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,420
reign from beginning to end.

5
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:23,700
Then the kings who came after him.

6
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,960
Get comfortable and let your eyes close.

7
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:33,420
If something from today is still turning over
in you, leave it in the comments — people

8
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:34,660
here pray through them.

9
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,840
Subscribe if these readings help you
sleep.

10
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:43,500
Lord, I got through today, and I am not
proud of all of it.

11
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:49,540
Some of what I did was right, and some of
it I would take back if taking back were a

12
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:50,480
thing that happened.

13
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:51,620
It isn't.

14
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:58,220
So I am lying here with it, going over
the same few minutes, as though going over them

15
00:00:58,260 --> 00:00:59,440
again would move them.

16
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:02,760
I am not asking you to undo anything
tonight.

17
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,560
I am asking you to hold the room steady
while I stop holding it.

18
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:14,820
Let the long account of a king go past
me slowly — his good years and his worst ones,

19
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:21,700
the grief he could not argue his way out
of, all of it already finished and told without

20
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:22,640
hurry.

21
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,520
I don't need to take a lesson from it.

22
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:28,700
I need something that keeps going while I
stop.

23
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,040
Take the tightness out of my jaw and out
of my hands.

24
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:36,460
Let my breathing drop below my thinking.

25
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:43,080
And be gentle tonight with everyone else
lying awake over the same few minutes.

26
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:43,900
Amen.

27
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:48,280
Second Samuel, chapter one.

28
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:53,560
After the death of Saul, when David
had returned from the slaughter of the Amalekites,

29
00:01:54,260 --> 00:02:00,900
and David had stayed two days in Ziklag,
on the third day, behold, a man came

30
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:05,740
out of the camp from Saul, with his
clothes torn and earth on his head.

31
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:09,980
When he came to David, he fell to the
earth and showed respect.

32
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:13,620
David said to him, “Where do you come
from?”

33
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,640
He said to him, “I have escaped out of the
camp of Israel.”

34
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:20,800
David said to him, “How did it go?

35
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,340
Please tell me.”

36
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:28,800
He answered, “The people have fled from the
battle, and many of the people also have

37
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,940
fallen and are dead.

38
00:02:30,295 --> 00:02:33,315
Saul and Jonathan his son are dead also.”

39
00:02:34,235 --> 00:02:40,395
David said to the young man who told him,
“How do you know that Saul and Jonathan his

40
00:02:40,435 --> 00:02:41,335
son are dead?”

41
00:02:42,175 --> 00:02:49,195
The young man who told him said, “As
I happened by chance on Mount Gilboa, behold,

42
00:02:49,835 --> 00:02:55,795
Saul was leaning on his spear; and
behold, the chariots and the horsemen followed close

43
00:02:55,835 --> 00:02:56,735
