44
00:02:56,775 --> 00:03:01,015
When he looked behind him, he saw me and
called to me.

45
00:03:01,775 --> 00:03:03,815
I answered, ‘Here I am.’

46
00:03:04,195 --> 00:03:06,255
He said to me, ‘Who are you?’

47
00:03:06,935 --> 00:03:10,135
I answered him, ‘I am an Amalekite.’

48
00:03:10,175 --> 00:03:16,635
He said to me, ‘Please stand beside me, and
kill me, for anguish has taken hold of me

49
00:03:16,995 --> 00:03:18,775
because my life lingers in me.’

50
00:03:19,475 --> 00:03:24,895
So I stood beside him and killed him, because
I was sure that he could not live after

51
00:03:24,935 --> 00:03:25,495
he had fallen.

52
00:03:25,535 --> 00:03:31,815
I took the crown that was on his head and
the bracelet that was on his arm, and have

53
00:03:31,855 --> 00:03:33,435
brought them here to my lord.”

54
00:03:34,415 --> 00:03:39,995
Then David took hold on his clothes and tore
them; and all the men who were with him

55
00:03:40,035 --> 00:03:40,935
did likewise.

56
00:03:41,575 --> 00:03:48,315
They mourned, wept, and fasted until evening
for Saul and for Jonathan his son, and

57
00:03:48,355 --> 00:03:53,835
for the people of the LORD, and for the
house of Israel, because they had fallen by the

58
00:03:53,875 --> 00:03:54,775
sword.

59
00:03:55,155 --> 00:03:59,255
David said to the young man who told him,
“Where are you from?”

60
00:04:00,055 --> 00:04:05,255
He answered, “I am the son of a foreigner,
an Amalekite.”

61
00:04:05,295 --> 00:04:11,655
David said to him, “Why were you not afraid
to stretch out your hand to destroy the LORD’s

62
00:04:11,695 --> 00:04:12,595
anointed?”

63
00:04:12,815 --> 00:04:17,855
David called one of the young men and
said, “Go near, and cut him down!”

64
