He struck him so that he died.

65
00:04:20,375 --> 00:04:26,815
David said to him, “Your blood be on your
head, for your mouth has testified against

66
00:04:26,855 --> 00:04:34,035
you, saying, ‘I have slain the
LORD’s anointed.’” David lamented with this lamentation

67
00:04:34,075 --> 00:04:40,015
over Saul and over Jonathan his son (and
he commanded them to teach the children of Judah

68
00:04:40,055 --> 00:04:47,195
the song of the bow; behold, it is
written in the book of Jashar): “Your glory, Israel,

69
00:04:47,675 --> 00:04:49,495
was slain on your high places!

70
00:04:49,535 --> 00:04:51,515
How the mighty have fallen!

71
00:04:52,395 --> 00:04:53,695
Don’t tell it in Gath.

72
00:04:54,038 --> 00:04:59,978
Don’t publish it in the streets of
Ashkelon, lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice,

73
00:05:01,298 --> 00:05:04,058
