80
00:05:37,698 --> 00:05:39,718
In their death, they were not divided.

81
00:05:40,658 --> 00:05:42,178
They were swifter than eagles.

82
00:05:43,018 --> 00:05:44,318
They were stronger than lions.

83
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:51,778
You daughters of Israel, weep over Saul,
who clothed you delicately in scarlet,

84
00:05:52,358 --> 00:05:54,658
who put ornaments of gold on your
clothing.

85
00:05:55,778 --> 00:05:58,558
How the mighty have fallen in the middle
of the battle!

86
00:05:59,098 --> 00:06:01,458
Jonathan was slain on your high places.

87
00:06:02,458 --> 00:06:04,738
I am distressed for you, my brother
Jonathan.

88
00:06:05,858 --> 00:06:07,878
You have been very pleasant to me.

89
00:06:08,318 --> 00:06:12,578
Your love to me was wonderful, surpassing
the love of women.

90
00:06:13,578 --> 00:06:17,878
How the mighty have fallen, and the
weapons of war have perished!”

91
00:06:18,478 --> 00:06:21,178
Second Samuel, chapter two.

92
00:06:21,218 --> 00:06:27,718
After this, David enquired of the LORD,
saying, “Shall I go up into any of the

93
00:06:27,758 --> 00:06:28,658
cities of Judah?”

94
00:06:29,678 --> 00:06:31,958
The LORD said to him, “Go up.”

95
00:06:32,878 --> 00:06:35,758
David said, “Where shall I go up?”

96
00:06:36,638 --> 00:06:38,158
He said, “To Hebron.”

97
00:06:38,778 --> 00:06:45,238
So David went up there with his two wives,
Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail

98
00:06:45,278 --> 00:06:48,238
the wife of Nabal the Carmelite.

99
00:06:48,278 --> 00:06:52,758
David brought up his men who were with
him, every man with his household.

100
00:06:53,938 --> 00:06:56,058
They lived in the cities of Hebron.

101
00:06:56,618 --> 00:07:02,098
The men of Judah came, and there they
anointed David king over the house of Judah.

102
00:07:03,138 --> 00:07:08,278
They told David, “The men of Jabesh Gilead
were those who buried Saul.”

103
00:07:09,038 --> 00:07:15,738
David sent messengers to the men of Jabesh
Gilead, and said to them, “Blessed are you

104
00:07:15,778 --> 00:07:22,538
by the LORD, that you have shown this kindness
to your lord, even to Saul, and have buried

105
00:07:22,578 --> 00:07:22,898
him.

106
00:07:22,938 --> 00:07:28,038
Now may the LORD show loving kindness and
truth to you.

107
00:07:28,307 --> 00:07:33,287
I also will reward you for this kindness,
because you have done this thing.

108
00:07:34,047 --> 00:07:40,727
Now therefore let your hands be strong, and
be valiant; for Saul your lord is dead,

109
00:07:41,387 --> 00:07:45,207
and also the house of Judah have anointed
me king over them.”

110
00:07:45,927 --> 00:07:52,387
Now Abner the son of Ner, captain of
Saul’s army, had taken Ishbosheth the son

111
00:07:52,427 --> 00:07:56,317
of Saul and brought him over to Mahanaim.

112
00:07:56,357 --> 00:08:03,587
He made him king over Gilead, over the
Ashurites, over Jezreel, over Ephraim,

113
00:08:03,627 --> 00:08:06,087
over Benjamin, and over all Israel.

114
00:08:06,127 --> 00:08:13,707
Ishbosheth, Saul’s son, was forty years old
when he began to reign over Israel, and

115
00:08:13,747 --> 00:08:14,967
he reigned two years.

116
00:08:16,087 --> 00:08:18,027
But the house of Judah followed David.

117
00:08:19,007 --> 00:08:25,397
The time that David was king in Hebron over
the house of Judah was seven years and six

118
00:08:25,437 --> 00:08:26,337
months.

119
00:08:26,497 --> 00:08:33,237
Abner the son of Ner, and the servants of
Ishbosheth the son of Saul, went out

120
00:08:33,277 --> 00:08:36,157
from Mahanaim to Gibeon.

121
00:08:36,197 --> 00:08:43,097
Joab the son of Zeruiah and David’s servants went
out, and met them by the pool of Gibeon;

122
00:08:43,137 --> 00:08:49,337
and they sat down, the one on the one side
of the pool and the other on the other side

123
00:08:49,377 --> 00:08:49,857
of the pool.

124
00:08:49,897 --> 00:08:56,137
Abner said to Joab, “Please let the young
men arise and compete before us!”

125
00:08:57,057 --> 00:08:59,717
Joab said, “Let them arise!”

126
00:09:00,897 --> 00:09:07,377
Then they arose and went over by number:
twelve for Benjamin and for Ishbosheth the son

127
00:09:07,417 --> 00:09:10,037
of Saul, and twelve of David’s servants.

128
00:09:10,937 --> 00:09:16,077
They each caught his opponent by the head
and thrust his sword in his fellow’s side;

129
00:09:16,677 --> 00:09:18,117
so they fell down together.

130
00:09:19,237 --> 00:09:24,617
Therefore that place in Gibeon was called
Helkath Hazzurim.

131
00:09:24,657 --> 00:09:30,977
The battle was very severe that day; and
Abner was beaten, and the men of Israel, before

132
00:09:31,017 --> 00:09:31,917
David’s servants.

133
00:09:32,677 --> 00:09:38,497
The three sons of Zeruiah were there:
Joab, Abishai, and Asahel.

134
00:09:39,477 --> 00:09:42,497
Asahel was as light of foot as a wild
gazelle.

135
00:09:43,517 --> 00:09:45,077
Asahel pursued Abner.

136
00:09:45,817 --> 00:09:49,777
He didn’t turn to the right hand or to the
left from following Abner.

137
00:09:50,177 --> 00:09:54,557
Then Abner looked behind him and said, “Is
that you, Asahel?”

138
00:09:55,017 --> 00:09:56,417
He answered, “It is.”

139
00:09:56,816 --> 00:10:03,336
Abner said to him, “Turn away to your
right hand or to your left, and grab one

140
00:10:03,376 --> 00:10:06,676
of the young men, and take his armour.”

141
00:10:06,716 --> 00:10:09,916
But Asahel would not turn away from
following him.

142
00:10:10,356 --> 00:10:14,636
Abner said again to Asahel, “Turn away
from following me.

143
00:10:15,596 --> 00:10:17,336
Why should I strike you to the ground?

144
00:10:18,176 --> 00:10:20,956
How then could I look Joab your brother in
the face?”

145
00:10:21,876 --> 00:10:24,316
However, he refused to turn away.

146
00:10:25,276 --> 00:10:31,216
Therefore Abner with the back end of the spear
struck him in the body, so that the spear

147
00:10:31,256 --> 00:10:36,496
came out behind him; and he fell down
there and died in the same place.

148
00:10:37,216 --> 00:10:42,136
As many as came to the place where Asahel
fell down and died stood still.

149
00:10:42,996 --> 00:10:45,896
But Joab and Abishai pursued Abner.

150
00:10:46,656 --> 00:10:52,816
The sun went down when they had come to
the hill of Ammah, that lies before Giah by the

151
00:10:52,856 --> 00:10:54,676
way of the wilderness of Gibeon.

152
00:10:55,216 --> 00:11:01,176
The children of Benjamin gathered themselves
together after Abner and became one band,

153
00:11:01,216 --> 00:11:03,616
and stood on the top of a hill.

154
00:11:04,756 --> 00:11:10,236
Then Abner called to Joab, and said,
“Shall the sword devour forever?

155
00:11:11,056 --> 00:11:14,196
Don’t you know that it will be bitterness
in the latter end?

156
00:11:14,796 --> 00:11:20,276
How long will it be then, before you
ask the people to return from following their brothers?”

157
00:11:21,396 --> 00:11:28,156
Joab said, “As God lives, if you had not
spoken, surely then in the morning the

158
00:11:28,196 --> 00:11:31,736
people would have gone away, and not each
followed his brother.”

159
00:11:32,856 --> 00:11:39,116
So Joab blew the trumpet; and all the
people stood still and pursued Israel no more,

160
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:41,156
and they fought no more.

161
00:11:42,336 --> 00:11:47,956
Abner and his men went all that night
through the Arabah; and they passed over the Jordan,

162
00:11:47,996 --> 00:11:52,176
and went through all Bithron, and came to
Mahanaim.

163
00:11:53,356 --> 00:11:58,596
Joab returned from following Abner; and when
he had gathered all the people together,

164
00:11:58,636 --> 00:12:02,496
nineteen men of David’s and Asahel were
missing.

165
00:12:03,596 --> 00:12:08,056
But David’s servants had struck Benjamin Abner’s
men so that three hundred and sixty

166
00:12:08,096 --> 00:12:09,756
men died.

167
00:12:10,676 --> 00:12:15,856
They took up Asahel and buried him in
the tomb of his father, which was in Bethlehem.

168
00:12:16,756 --> 00:12:21,936
Joab and his men went all night, and the
day broke on them at Hebron.

169
00:12:22,523 --> 00:12:25,583
Second Samuel, chapter three.

170
00:12:25,623 --> 00:12:30,263
Now there was long war between Saul’s
house and David’s house.

171
00:12:31,103 --> 00:12:37,323
David grew stronger and stronger, but
Saul’s house grew weaker and weaker.

172
00:12:38,603 --> 00:12:40,923
Sons were born to David in Hebron.

173
00:12:41,383 --> 00:12:48,243
His firstborn was Amnon, of Ahinoam the
Jezreelitess; and his second, Chileab,

174
00:12:48,283 --> 00:12:54,743
of Abigail the wife of Nabal the
Carmelite; and the third, Absalom

175
00:12:54,783 --> 00:13:01,523
the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai
king of Geshur; and the fourth, Adonijah the

176
00:13:01,563 --> 00:13:08,823
son of Haggith; and the fifth, Shephatiah
the son of Abital; and the sixth, Ithream,

177
00:13:08,863 --> 00:13:10,883
of Eglah, David’s wife.

178
00:13:11,563 --> 00:13:13,643
These were born to David in Hebron.

179
00:13:13,683 --> 00:13:20,463
While there was war between Saul’s house
and David’s house, Abner made himself strong

180
00:13:20,503 --> 00:13:21,663
in Saul’s house.

181
00:13:22,683 --> 00:13:29,123
Now Saul had a concubine, whose name
was Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah; and Ishbosheth

182
00:13:29,163 --> 00:13:33,743
said to Abner, “Why have you gone in to my
father’s concubine?”

183
00:13:34,343 --> 00:13:41,083
Then Abner was very angry about Ishbosheth’s
words, and said, “Am I a dog’s

184
00:13:41,123 --> 00:13:42,543
head that belongs to Judah?

185
00:13:43,443 --> 00:13:49,163
Today I show kindness to your father Saul’s
house, to his brothers, and to his friends,

186
00:13:49,863 --> 00:13:54,943
and have not delivered you into the hand of
David; and yet you charge me today with a

187
00:13:54,983 --> 00:13:56,603
fault concerning this woman!

188
00:13:57,503 --> 00:14:04,323
God do so to Abner, and more also, if, as
the LORD has sworn to David, I

189
00:14:04,363 --> 00:14:10,783
don’t do even so to him: to transfer the
kingdom from Saul’s house, and to set up David’s

190
00:14:10,823 --> 00:14:15,923
