214
00:15:59,913 --> 00:16:04,093
So Abner came to David to Hebron, and
twenty men with him.

215
00:16:04,893 --> 00:16:07,953
David made Abner and the men who were with
him a feast.

216
00:16:08,653 --> 00:16:15,033
Abner said to David, “I will arise and go,
and will gather all Israel to my lord the

217
00:16:15,073 --> 00:16:20,633
king, that they may make a covenant with you,
and that you may reign over all that your

218
00:16:20,673 --> 00:16:21,573
soul desires.”

219
00:16:22,633 --> 00:16:25,973
David sent Abner away; and he went in
peace.

220
00:16:26,613 --> 00:16:32,953
Behold, David’s servants and Joab came from a
raid and brought in a great plunder with

221
00:16:32,993 --> 00:16:39,553
them; but Abner was not with David in Hebron,
for he had sent him away, and he had

222
00:16:39,593 --> 00:16:40,493
gone in peace.

223
00:16:40,893 --> 00:16:46,833
When Joab and all the army who was with
him had come, they told Joab, “Abner the son

224
00:16:46,873 --> 00:16:52,153
of Ner came to the king, and he has sent
him away, and he has gone in peace.”

225
00:16:53,193 --> 00:16:56,913
Then Joab came to the king and said, “What
have you done?

226
00:16:57,733 --> 00:16:59,573
Behold, Abner came to you.

227
00:17:00,113 --> 00:17:03,933
Why is it that you have sent him away, and
he is already gone?

228
00:17:04,793 --> 00:17:07,453
You know Abner the son of Ner.

229
00:17:07,493 --> 00:17:13,453
He came to deceive you, and to know your
going out and your coming in, and to know all

230
00:17:13,493 --> 00:17:14,393
that you do.”

231
00:17:14,522 --> 00:17:20,522
When Joab had come out from David, he
sent messengers after Abner, and they brought him

232
00:17:20,562 --> 00:17:24,482
back from the well of Sirah; but David
didn’t know it.

233
00:17:24,842 --> 00:17:30,882
When Abner had returned to Hebron, Joab took
him aside into the middle of the gate to

234
00:17:30,922 --> 00:17:36,902
speak with him quietly, and struck him there in
the body, so that he died for the blood

235
00:17:36,942 --> 00:17:38,182
of Asahel his brother.

236
00:17:38,222 --> 00:17:44,982
Afterward, when David heard it, he said,
“I and my kingdom are guiltless

237
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:50,082
before the LORD forever of the blood of
Abner the son of Ner.

238
00:17:50,122 --> 00:17:54,242
Let it fall on the head of Joab and on all
his father’s house.

239
00:17:54,882 --> 00:18:01,302
Let there not fail from the house of Joab
one who has a discharge, or who is a leper,

240
00:18:01,862 --> 00:18:07,662
or who leans on a staff, or who falls by
the sword, or who lacks bread.”

241
00:18:08,082 --> 00:18:14,182
So Joab and Abishai his brother killed
Abner, because he had killed their brother Asahel

242
00:18:14,222 --> 00:18:15,522
at Gibeon in the battle.

243
00:18:16,162 --> 00:18:22,842
David said to Joab and to all the people
who were with him, “Tear your clothes, and clothe

244
00:18:22,882 --> 00:18:26,462
yourselves with sackcloth, and mourn in
front of Abner.”

245
00:18:26,822 --> 00:18:29,162
King David followed the bier.

246
00:18:29,202 --> 00:18:35,642
They buried Abner in Hebron; and the king
lifted up his voice and wept at Abner’s grave;

247
00:18:36,502 --> 00:18:37,942
and all the people wept.

248
00:18:38,442 --> 00:18:44,042
The king lamented for Abner, and said,
“Should Abner die as a fool dies?

249
00:18:44,982 --> 00:18:48,622
Your hands weren’t bound, and your feet
weren’t put into fetters.

250
00:18:49,582 --> 00:18:53,722
As a man falls before the children of
iniquity, so you fell.”

251
00:18:54,102 --> 00:18:56,162
All the people wept again over him.

252
00:18:56,762 --> 00:19:02,682
All the people came to urge David to eat
bread while it was yet day; but David swore,

253
00:19:03,002 --> 00:19:10,182
saying, “God do so to me, and more also,
if I taste bread or anything else, until

254
00:19:10,222 --> 00:19:11,282
the sun goes down.”

255
00:19:11,702 --> 00:19:17,002
All the people took notice of it, and
it pleased them, as whatever the king did pleased

256
00:19:17,042 --> 00:19:17,942
all the people.

257
00:19:18,582 --> 00:19:24,982
So all the people and all Israel understood that
day that it was not of the king to kill

258
00:19:25,022 --> 00:19:27,522
Abner the son of Ner.

259
00:19:27,562 --> 00:19:33,542
The king said to his servants, “Don’t you know
that a prince and a great man has fallen

260
00:19:33,582 --> 00:19:34,642
today in Israel?

261
00:19:35,622 --> 00:19:38,342
I am weak today, though anointed king.

262
00:19:38,775 --> 00:19:43,035
These men, the sons of Zeruiah are too
hard for me.

263
00:19:43,915 --> 00:19:47,715
May the LORD reward the evildoer according
to his wickedness.”

264
00:19:47,755 --> 00:19:51,455
Second Samuel, chapter four.

265
00:19:51,495 --> 00:19:58,035
When Saul’s son heard that Abner was dead
in Hebron, his hands became feeble, and

266
00:19:58,075 --> 00:19:59,815
all the Israelites were troubled.

267
00:20:00,675 --> 00:20:04,075
Saul’s son had two men who were captains
of raiding bands.

268
00:20:04,975 --> 00:20:11,475
The name of one was Baanah and the name of
the other Rechab, the sons of Rimmon the

269
00:20:11,515 --> 00:20:17,855
Beerothite, of the children of Benjamin (for
Beeroth also is considered a part of Benjamin;

270
00:20:18,835 --> 00:20:24,275
and the Beerothites fled to Gittaim, and
have lived as foreigners there until today).

271
00:20:24,755 --> 00:20:28,995
Now Jonathan, Saul’s son, had a son who
was lame in his feet.

272
00:20:29,555 --> 00:20:35,355
He was five years old when the news
came about Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel; and

273
00:20:35,395 --> 00:20:37,195
his nurse picked him up and fled.

274
00:20:38,375 --> 00:20:41,615
As she hurried to flee, he fell and became
lame.

275
00:20:42,735 --> 00:20:44,915
His name was Mephibosheth.

276
00:20:44,955 --> 00:20:51,495
The sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, Rechab
and Baanah, went out and came at about

277
00:20:51,535 --> 00:20:56,615
the heat of the day to the house of
Ishbosheth as he took his rest at noon.

278
00:20:56,655 --> 00:21:02,415
They came there into the middle of the
house as though they would have fetched wheat,

279
00:21:03,255 --> 00:21:07,475
and they struck him in the body; and
Rechab and Baanah his brother escaped.

280
00:21:08,515 --> 00:21:14,195
Now when they came into the house as he
lay on his bed in his bedroom, they struck him,

281
00:21:14,535 --> 00:21:20,495
killed him, beheaded him, and took his head, and
went by the way of the Arabah all night.

282
00:21:20,535 --> 00:21:27,495
They brought the head of Ishbosheth to David
to Hebron, and said to the king, “Behold,

283
00:21:28,155 --> 00:21:33,595
the head of Ishbosheth, the son of Saul,
your enemy, who sought your life!

284
00:21:34,675 --> 00:21:39,175
The LORD has avenged my lord the king
today of Saul and of his offspring.”

285
00:21:39,759 --> 00:21:45,799
David answered Rechab and Baanah his brother,
the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, and

286
00:21:45,839 --> 00:21:53,299
said to them, “As the LORD lives, who
has redeemed my soul out of all adversity, when

287
00:21:53,339 --> 00:22:00,019
someone told me, ‘Behold, Saul is dead,’
thinking that he brought good news, I

288
00:22:00,059 --> 00:22:05,479
seized him and killed him in Ziklag, which
was the reward I gave him for his news.

289
00:22:06,819 --> 00:22:12,199
How much more, when wicked men have slain
a righteous person in his own house on his

290
00:22:12,239 --> 00:22:18,299
bed, should I not now require his blood
from your hand, and rid the earth of you?”

291
00:22:18,859 --> 00:22:24,319
David commanded his young men, and they killed
them, cut off their hands and their feet,

292
00:22:24,839 --> 00:22:27,259
and hanged them up beside the pool in
Hebron.

293
00:22:27,959 --> 00:22:33,319
But they took the head of Ishbosheth and
buried it in Abner’s grave in Hebron.

294
00:22:33,359 --> 00:22:36,519
Second Samuel, chapter five.

295
00:22:36,559 --> 00:22:43,099
Then all the tribes of Israel came to
David at Hebron and spoke, saying, “Behold, we

296
00:22:43,139 --> 00:22:44,799
are your bone and your flesh.

297
00:22:45,979 --> 00:22:52,459
In times past, when Saul was king over us,
it was you who led Israel out and in.

298
00:22:53,139 --> 00:22:58,659
The LORD said to you, ‘You will be shepherd
of my people Israel, and you will be prince

299
00:22:58,699 --> 00:23:05,239
over Israel.’” So all the elders of Israel
came to the king to Hebron, and King

300
00:23:05,279 --> 00:23:10,959
David made a covenant with them in Hebron
before the LORD; and they anointed David king

301
00:23:10,999 --> 00:23:11,899
over Israel.

302
00:23:12,399 --> 00:23:17,879
David was thirty years old when he began
to reign, and he reigned forty years.

303
00:23:18,739 --> 00:23:25,159
In Hebron he reigned over Judah seven years
and six months, and in Jerusalem he reigned

304
00:23:25,199 --> 00:23:28,179
thirty-three years over all Israel and
Judah.

305
00:23:28,919 --> 00:23:34,079
The king and his men went to
Jerusalem against the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the

306
00:23:34,119 --> 00:23:40,119
land, who spoke to David, saying, “The blind
and the lame will keep you out of here,”

307
00:23:40,679 --> 00:23:42,919
thinking, “David can’t come in here.”

308
00:23:43,599 --> 00:23:46,639
Nevertheless David took the stronghold of
Zion.

309
00:23:47,359 --> 00:23:48,699
This is David’s city.

310
00:23:49,299 --> 00:23:56,219
David said on that day, “Whoever strikes the
Jebusites, let him go up to the watercourse

311
00:23:56,259 --> 00:24:00,979
and strike those lame and blind, who are
hated by David’s soul.”

312
00:24:01,356 --> 00:24:06,536
Therefore they say, “The blind and the
lame can’t come into the house.”

313
00:24:07,636 --> 00:24:11,736
David lived in the stronghold, and called
it David’s city.

314
00:24:12,616 --> 00:24:15,736
David built around from Millo and inward.

315
00:24:16,876 --> 00:24:22,456
David grew greater and greater, for the
LORD, the God of Armies, was with him.

316
00:24:23,316 --> 00:24:29,596
Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to
David, with cedar trees, carpenters, and masons;

317
00:24:29,636 --> 00:24:31,896
and they built David a house.

318
00:24:32,896 --> 00:24:38,756
David perceived that the LORD had established him
king over Israel, and that he had exalted

319
00:24:38,796 --> 00:24:41,556
his kingdom for his people Israel’s sake.

320
00:24:42,236 --> 00:24:48,316
David took more concubines and wives for
himself out of Jerusalem, after he had come

321
00:24:48,356 --> 00:24:52,436
from Hebron; and more sons and daughters
were born to David.

322
00:24:53,076 --> 00:25:00,136
These are the names of those who were
born to him in Jerusalem: Shammua, Shobab, Nathan,

323
00:25:01,116 --> 00:25:07,686
Solomon, Ibhar, Elishua, Nepheg, Japhia,
Elishama,

324
00:25:07,726 --> 00:25:10,196
Eliada, and Eliphelet.

325
00:25:10,236 --> 00:25:16,276
When the Philistines heard that they had
anointed David king over Israel, all the Philistines

326
00:25:16,316 --> 00:25:23,156
went up to seek David, but David heard
about it and went down to the stronghold.

327
00:25:23,196 --> 00:25:28,396
Now the Philistines had come and spread
themselves in the valley of Rephaim.

328
00:25:28,436 --> 00:25:33,936
David enquired of the LORD, saying, “Shall
I go up against the Philistines?

329
00:25:34,656 --> 00:25:36,576
Will you deliver them into my hand?”

330
00:25:37,496 --> 00:25:43,456
The LORD said to David, “Go up; for
I will certainly deliver the Philistines into your

331
00:25:43,496 --> 00:25:44,256
hand.”

332
00:25:44,296 --> 00:25:48,496
David came to Baal Perazim, and David
struck them there.

333
00:25:49,156 --> 00:25:55,036
Then he said, “The LORD has broken my
enemies before me, like the breach of waters.”

334
00:25:56,016 --> 00:26:00,516
Therefore he called the name of that place
Baal Perazim.

335
00:26:00,556 --> 00:26:05,336
They left their images there, and David
and his men took them away.

336
00:26:05,816 --> 00:26:11,456
The Philistines came up yet again and
spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim.

337
00:26:11,496 --> 00:26:16,596
When David enquired of the LORD, he said,
“You shall not go up.

338
00:26:17,416 --> 00:26:21,796
Circle around behind them, and attack them
in front of the mulberry trees.

339
00:26:22,328 --> 00:26:27,888
When you hear the sound of marching in
the tops of the mulberry trees, then stir yourself

340
00:26:27,928 --> 00:26:33,808
up; for then the LORD has gone out
before you to strike the army of the Philistines.”

341
00:26:35,008 --> 00:26:41,208
David did so, as the LORD commanded him,
and struck the Philistines all the way from

342
00:26:41,248 --> 00:26:42,448
Geba to Gezer.

343
00:26:42,488 --> 00:26:45,908
Second Samuel, chapter six.

344
00:26:45,948 --> 00:26:51,848
David again gathered together all the
chosen men of Israel, thirty thousand.

345
00:26:51,888 --> 00:26:57,528
David arose and went with all the people
who were with him from Baale Judah, to bring

346
00:26:57,568 --> 00:27:03,828
up from there God’s ark, which is called by
the Name, even the name of the LORD of Armies

347
00:27:03,868 --> 00:27:05,548
who sits above the cherubim.

348
00:27:06,088 --> 00:27:12,008
They set God’s ark on a new cart, and
brought it out of Abinadab’s house that was on

349
00:27:12,048 --> 00:27:18,488
the hill; and Uzzah and Ahio, the sons of
Abinadab, drove the new cart.

350
00:27:19,768 --> 00:27:26,308
They brought it out of Abinadab’s house which
was in the hill, with God’s ark; and Ahio

351
00:27:26,348 --> 00:27:27,568
went before the ark.

352
00:27:28,268 --> 00:27:33,608
David and all the house of Israel played
before the LORD with all kinds of instruments

353
00:27:33,648 --> 00:27:40,548
made of cypress wood, with harps,
with stringed instruments, with tambourines, with

354
00:27:40,588 --> 00:27:43,308
castanets, and with cymbals.

355
00:27:43,348 --> 00:27:48,928
When they came to the threshing floor of
Nacon, Uzzah reached for God’s ark and took

356
00:27:48,968 --> 00:27:51,228
hold of it, for the cattle stumbled.

357
00:27:52,468 --> 00:27:58,528
The LORD’s anger burnt against Uzzah, and
God struck him there for his error; and he

358
00:27:58,568 --> 00:28:00,108
died there by God’s ark.

359
00:28:00,808 --> 00:28:06,588
David was displeased because the LORD had
broken out against Uzzah; and he called that

360
00:28:06,628 --> 00:28:08,868
place Perez Uzzah to this day.

361
00:28:09,768 --> 00:28:16,108
David was afraid of the LORD that day; and
he said, “How could the LORD’s ark come to

362
00:28:16,148 --> 00:28:17,048
me?”

363
00:28:17,228 --> 00:28:22,988
So David would not move the LORD’s ark to
be with him in David’s city; but David carried

364
00:28:23,028 --> 00:28:26,448
it aside into Obed-Edom the Gittite’s
house.

365
00:28:27,188 --> 00:28:33,648
The LORD’s ark remained in Obed-Edom the
Gittite’s house three months; and the LORD blessed

366
00:28:33,688 --> 00:28:36,008
Obed-Edom and all his house.

367
00:28:36,648 --> 00:28:42,648
King David was told, “The LORD has blessed
the house of Obed-Edom, and all that belongs

368
00:28:42,688 --> 00:28:44,788
to him, because of God’s ark.”

369
00:28:45,133 --> 00:28:51,013
So David went and brought up God’s ark
from the house of Obed-Edom into David’s city

370
00:28:51,053 --> 00:28:51,953
with joy.

371
00:28:52,893 --> 00:28:59,773
When those who bore the LORD’s ark had gone
six paces, he sacrificed an ox and a fattened

372
00:28:59,813 --> 00:29:00,713
calf.

373
00:29:01,073 --> 00:29:07,533
David danced before the LORD with all his
might; and David was clothed in a linen ephod.

374
00:29:08,153 --> 00:29:14,173
So David and all the house of Israel
brought up the LORD’s ark with shouting and with

375
00:29:14,213 --> 00:29:15,313
the sound of the trumpet.

376
00:29:16,473 --> 00:29:22,493
As the LORD’s ark came into David’s city,
Michal the daughter of Saul looked out through

377
00:29:22,533 --> 00:29:28,653
the window and saw King David leaping and
dancing before the LORD; and she despised him

378
00:29:28,693 --> 00:29:29,593
in her heart.

379
00:29:30,293 --> 00:29:35,593
They brought in the LORD’s ark, and set it
in its place in the middle of the tent that

380
00:29:35,633 --> 00:29:41,513
David had pitched for it; and David
offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before

381
00:29:41,553 --> 00:29:42,453
the LORD.

382
00:29:42,613 --> 00:29:47,793
When David had finished offering the burnt
offering and the peace offerings, he blessed

383
00:29:47,833 --> 00:29:50,353
the people in the name of the LORD of
Armies.

384
00:29:51,253 --> 00:29:57,573
He gave to all the people, even amongst
the whole multitude of Israel, both to men and

385
00:29:57,613 --> 00:30:02,153
women, to everyone a portion of bread,
dates, and raisins.

386
00:30:02,713 --> 00:30:06,133
So all the people departed, each to his
own house.

387
00:30:07,133 --> 00:30:09,333
Then David returned to bless his
household.

388
00:30:09,373 --> 00:30:15,853
Michal the daughter of Saul came out to
meet David, and said, “How glorious

389
00:30:15,893 --> 00:30:21,613
the king of Israel was today, who uncovered
himself today in the eyes of his servants’

390
00:30:21,973 --> 00:30:26,153
maids, as one of the vain fellows
shamelessly uncovers himself!”

391
00:30:26,853 --> 00:30:33,093
David said to Michal, “It was before the
LORD, who chose me above your father, and above

392
00:30:33,133 --> 00:30:38,333
all his house, to appoint me prince over
the people of the LORD, over Israel.

393
00:30:39,393 --> 00:30:41,993
Therefore I will celebrate before the
LORD.

394
00:30:42,813 --> 00:30:47,693
I will be yet more undignified than this,
and will be worthless in my own sight.

395
00:30:48,453 --> 00:30:51,293
But the maids of whom you have spoken will
honour me.”

396
00:30:51,333 --> 00:30:56,533
Michal the daughter of Saul had no child
to the day of her death.

397
00:30:56,573 --> 00:30:59,233
Second Samuel, chapter seven.

398
00:31:00,153 --> 00:31:05,793
When the king lived in his house, and the
LORD had given him rest from all his enemies

399
00:31:05,833 --> 00:31:12,453
all around, the king said to Nathan the
prophet, “See now, I dwell in

400
00:31:12,493 --> 00:31:16,453
a house of cedar, but God’s ark dwells
within curtains.”

401
00:31:17,273 --> 00:31:23,753
Nathan said to the king, “Go, do all that
is in your heart, for the LORD is with you.”

402
00:31:24,513 --> 00:31:31,273
That same night, the LORD’s word came to
Nathan, saying, “Go and tell my servant David,

403
00:31:32,173 --> 00:31:36,053
‘The LORD says, “Should you build me a
house for me to dwell in?

404
00:31:36,453 --> 00:31:41,353
For I have not lived in a house since
the day that I brought the children of Israel up

405
00:31:41,393 --> 00:31:47,493
out of Egypt, even to this day, but have
moved around in a tent and in a tabernacle.

406
00:31:48,033 --> 00:31:53,853
In all places in which I have walked with
all the children of Israel, did I say a word

407
00:31:53,893 --> 00:31:59,253
to anyone from the tribes of Israel whom
I commanded to be shepherd of my people Israel,

408
00:31:59,813 --> 00:32:05,773
saying, ‘Why have you not built me a house
of cedar?’”’ Now therefore tell my servant

409
00:32:05,813 --> 00:32:12,473
David this: ‘The LORD of Armies says, “I
took you from the sheep pen, from following

410
00:32:12,513 --> 00:32:16,233
the sheep, to be prince over my people,
over Israel.

411
00:32:17,033 --> 00:32:22,213
I have been with you wherever you went,
and have cut off all your enemies from before

412
00:32:22,253 --> 00:32:22,953
you.

413
00:32:22,993 --> 00:32:27,993
I will make you a great name, like the
name of the great ones who are in the earth.

414
00:32:28,933 --> 00:32:34,733
I will appoint a place for my people
Israel, and will plant them, that they may dwell

415
00:32:34,773 --> 00:32:38,073
in their own place and be moved no more.

416
00:32:38,713 --> 00:32:44,633
The children of wickedness will not afflict them
any more, as at the first, and as from

417
00:32:44,673 --> 00:32:48,313
the day that I commanded judges to be over
my people Israel.

418
00:32:48,933 --> 00:32:51,933
I will cause you to rest from all your
enemies.

419
00:32:53,033 --> 00:32:57,013
Moreover the LORD tells you that the LORD
will make you a house.

420
00:32:57,053 --> 00:33:03,173
When your days are fulfilled and you sleep
with your fathers, I will set up your offspring

421
00:33:03,213 --> 00:33:08,833
after you, who will proceed out of your
body, and I will establish his kingdom.

422
00:33:09,793 --> 00:33:15,613
He will build a house for my name, and
I will establish the throne of his kingdom forever.

423
00:33:18,293 --> 00:33:19,433
I will be his father, and he will be my
son.

424
00:33:19,849 --> 00:33:26,369
If he commits iniquity, I will chasten him with
the rod of men and with the stripes of

425
00:33:26,409 --> 00:33:32,769
the children of men; but my loving kindness will
not depart from him, as I took it from

426
00:33:32,809 --> 00:33:35,549
Saul, whom I put away before you.

427
00:33:36,189 --> 00:33:40,729
Your house and your kingdom will be made
sure forever before you.

428
00:33:41,389 --> 00:33:48,309
Your throne will be established forever.”’” Nathan
spoke to David all these words, and

429
00:33:48,349 --> 00:33:49,949
according to all this vision.

430
00:33:50,989 --> 00:33:57,789
Then David the king went in and sat before
the LORD; and he said, “Who am I, Lord

431
00:33:57,829 --> 00:34:01,969
GOD, and what is my house, that you have
brought me this far?

432
00:34:02,669 --> 00:34:08,949
This was yet a small thing in your eyes,
