was over the Cherethites and the Pelethites;

496
00:39:17,866 --> 00:39:19,646
and David’s sons were chief ministers.

497
00:39:19,686 --> 00:39:23,746
Second Samuel, chapter nine.

498
00:39:23,786 --> 00:39:29,606
David said, “Is there yet any who is left
of Saul’s house, that I may show him kindness

499
00:39:29,646 --> 00:39:31,086
for Jonathan’s sake?”

500
00:39:32,206 --> 00:39:37,566
There was of Saul’s house a servant whose
name was Ziba, and they called him to David;

501
00:39:38,206 --> 00:39:40,806
and the king said to him, “Are you Ziba?”

502
00:39:41,386 --> 00:39:43,346
He said, “I am your servant.”

503
00:39:44,526 --> 00:39:50,306
The king said, “Is there not yet any of
Saul’s house, that I may show the kindness of

504
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:51,246
God to him?”

505
00:39:52,066 --> 00:39:57,886
Ziba said to the king, “Jonathan still has
a son, who is lame in his feet.”

506
00:39:58,906 --> 00:40:01,346
The king said to him, “Where is he?”

507
00:40:02,046 --> 00:40:08,626
Ziba said to the king, “Behold, he is in
the house of Machir the son of Ammiel, in Lo

508
00:40:08,666 --> 00:40:09,566
Debar.”

509
00:40:10,166 --> 00:40:15,626
Then King David sent and brought him out of
the house of Machir the son of Ammiel, from

510
00:40:15,666 --> 00:40:16,566
Lo Debar.

511
00:40:17,326 --> 00:40:23,446
Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, the son
of Saul, came to David, fell on his face,

512
00:40:23,926 --> 00:40:24,826
and showed respect.

513
00:40:25,966 --> 00:40:28,226
David said, “Mephibosheth?”

514
00:40:28,586 --> 00:40:31,166
He answered, “Behold, your servant!”

515
00:40:31,648 --> 00:40:37,968
David said to him, “Don’t be afraid, for I
will surely show you kindness for Jonathan

516
00:40:38,008 --> 00:40:43,348
your father’s sake, and will restore to
you all the land of Saul your father.

517
00:40:44,088 --> 00:40:46,968
