586
00:46:09,647 --> 00:46:11,127
But David stayed at Jerusalem.

587
00:46:12,487 --> 00:46:18,147
At evening, David arose from his bed and
walked on the roof of the king’s house.

588
00:46:19,007 --> 00:46:24,887
From the roof, he saw a woman bathing, and
the woman was very beautiful to look at.

589
00:46:25,727 --> 00:46:28,407
David sent and enquired after the woman.

590
00:46:28,847 --> 00:46:35,447
One said, “Isn’t this Bathsheba, the
daughter of Eliam, Uriah the Hittite’s wife?”

591
00:46:36,547 --> 00:46:43,327
David sent messengers, and took her; and she came
in to him, and he lay with her (for

592
00:46:43,367 --> 00:46:47,947
