and she returned to her house.

593
00:46:48,747 --> 00:46:54,267
The woman conceived; and she sent and told
David, and said, “I am with child.”

594
00:46:55,087 --> 00:46:59,127
David sent to Joab, “Send me Uriah the
Hittite.”

595
00:47:00,407 --> 00:47:02,247
Joab sent Uriah to David.

596
00:47:03,347 --> 00:47:10,467
When Uriah had come to him, David asked him
how Joab did, and how the people fared, and

597
00:47:10,507 --> 00:47:11,867
how the war prospered.

598
00:47:12,227 --> 00:47:16,747
David said to Uriah, “Go down to your
house and wash your feet.”

599
00:47:17,407 --> 00:47:22,847
Uriah departed out of the king’s house, and
a gift from the king was sent after him.

600
00:47:23,787 --> 00:47:29,707
But Uriah slept at the door of the king’s
house with all the servants of his lord, and

601
00:47:29,747 --> 00:47:31,387
didn’t go down to his house.

602
00:47:31,727 --> 00:47:36,387
When they had told David, saying, “Uriah
didn’t go down to his house,”

603
00:47:36,601 --> 00:47:40,621
David said to Uriah, “Haven’t you come
from a journey?

604
00:47:41,561 --> 00:47:43,421
Why didn’t you go down to your house?”

605
00:47:44,661 --> 00:47:51,921
Uriah said to David, “The ark, Israel, and
Judah, are staying in tents; and

606
00:47:51,961 --> 00:47:57,201
my lord Joab and the servants of my lord
are encamped in the open field.

607
00:47:57,901 --> 00:48:02,941
Shall I then go into my house to eat and
to drink, and to lie with my wife?

608
00:48:03,761 --> 00:48:08,821
As you live, and as your soul lives, I
will not do this thing!”

609
00:48:09,681 --> 00:48:15,881
David said to Uriah, “Stay here today
also, and tomorrow I will let you depart.”

610
00:48:16,561 --> 00:48:20,321
So Uriah stayed in Jerusalem that day and
the next day.

611
00:48:21,041 --> 00:48:26,281
When David had called him, he ate and
drank before him; and he made him drunk.

612
00:48:27,341 --> 00:48:33,261
At evening, he went out to lie on his
bed with the servants of his lord, but didn’t go

613
00:48:33,301 --> 00:48:34,261
down to his house.

614
00:48:34,301 --> 00:48:40,221
In the morning, David wrote a letter to
Joab and sent it by the hand of Uriah.

615
00:48:40,581 --> 00:48:46,855
He wrote in the letter, saying, “Send Uriah
to the forefront of the hottest battle, and

616
00:48:46,895 --> 00:48:50,481
retreat from him, that he may be struck
and die.”

617
00:48:51,641 --> 00:48:58,461
When Joab kept watch on the city, he assigned
Uriah to the place where he knew that valiant

618
00:48:58,501 --> 00:48:59,401
men were.

619
00:48:59,601 --> 00:49:02,621
The men of the city went out and fought
with Joab.

620
00:49:03,281 --> 00:49:09,601
Some of the people fell, even of David’s
servants; and Uriah the Hittite died also.

621
00:49:10,541 --> 00:49:16,841
Then Joab sent and told David all the
things concerning the war; and he commanded the

622
00:49:16,881 --> 00:49:22,281
messenger, saying, “When you have finished
telling all the things concerning the war

623
00:49:22,321 --> 00:49:29,061
to the king, it shall be that, if the
king’s wrath arise, and he asks you, ‘Why

624
00:49:29,101 --> 00:49:31,381
did you go so near to the city to fight?

625
00:49:32,281 --> 00:49:34,801
Didn’t you know that they would shoot from
the wall?

626
00:49:35,441 --> 00:49:38,901
Who struck Abimelech the son of
Jerubbesheth?

627
00:49:38,941 --> 00:49:45,501
Didn’t a woman cast an upper millstone on him
from the wall, so that he died at Thebez?

628
00:49:45,541 --> 00:49:47,521
Why did you go so near the wall?’

629
00:49:48,361 --> 00:49:54,481
then you shall say, ‘Your servant Uriah
the Hittite is also dead.’” So the messenger

630
00:49:54,521 --> 00:49:59,241
went, and came and showed David all that
Joab had sent him for.

631
00:49:59,552 --> 00:50:05,812
The messenger said to David, “The men prevailed
against us, and came out to us into the

632
00:50:05,852 --> 00:50:09,932
field; and we were on them even to the
entrance of the gate.

633
00:50:11,032 --> 00:50:16,252
The shooters shot at your servants from off
the wall; and some of the king’s servants

634
00:50:16,292 --> 00:50:20,652
are dead, and your servant Uriah the
Hittite is also dead.”

635
00:50:21,312 --> 00:50:27,752
Then David said to the messenger, “Tell
Joab, ‘Don’t let this thing displease you, for

636
00:50:27,792 --> 00:50:30,292
the sword devours one as well as another.

637
00:50:31,152 --> 00:50:35,052
Make your battle stronger against the
city, and overthrow it.’

638
00:50:35,712 --> 00:50:36,612
Encourage him.”

639
00:50:37,212 --> 00:50:42,732
When Uriah’s wife heard that Uriah her
husband was dead, she mourned for her husband.

640
00:50:43,652 --> 00:50:49,392
When the mourning was past, David sent and
took her home to his house, and she became

641
00:50:49,432 --> 00:50:51,692
his wife and bore him a son.

642
00:50:52,452 --> 00:50:55,772
But the thing that David had done
displeased the LORD.

643
00:50:55,812 --> 00:50:58,792
Second Samuel, chapter twelve.

644
00:50:58,832 --> 00:51:00,532
The LORD sent Nathan to David.

645
00:51:01,552 --> 00:51:08,432
He came to him, and said to him, “There
were two men in one city: the one rich, and

646
00:51:08,472 --> 00:51:09,372
the other poor.

647
00:51:10,032 --> 00:51:16,632
The rich man had very many flocks and
herds, but the poor man had nothing, except one

648
00:51:16,672 --> 00:51:19,592
little ewe lamb, which he had bought and
raised.

649
00:51:20,432 --> 00:51:22,952
It grew up together with him and with his
children.

650
00:51:22,992 --> 00:51:29,612
It ate of his own food, drank of his own
cup, and lay in his bosom, and

651
00:51:29,652 --> 00:51:31,052
was like a daughter to him.

652
00:51:31,652 --> 00:51:36,972
A traveller came to the rich man, and he
didn’t want to take of his own flock and of

653
00:51:37,012 --> 00:51:42,792
his own herd to prepare for the wayfaring
man who had come to him, but took the poor

654
00:51:42,832 --> 00:51:46,552
man’s lamb and prepared it for the man who
had come to him.”

655
00:51:47,052 --> 00:51:53,732
David’s anger burnt hot against the man, and
he said to Nathan, “As the LORD lives, the

656
00:51:53,772 --> 00:51:56,132
man who has done this deserves to die!

657
00:51:56,952 --> 00:52:02,832
He must restore the lamb fourfold, because he
did this thing and because he had no pity!”

658
00:52:03,832 --> 00:52:06,472
Nathan said to David, “You are the man!

659
00:52:07,072 --> 00:52:14,352
This is what the LORD, the God of
Israel, says: ‘I anointed you king over Israel, and

660
00:52:14,392 --> 00:52:16,632
I delivered you out of the hand of Saul.

661
00:52:17,106 --> 00:52:22,886
I gave you your master’s house and your
master’s wives into your bosom, and gave you

662
00:52:22,926 --> 00:52:28,746
the house of Israel and of Judah; and if
that would have been too little, I would have

663
00:52:28,786 --> 00:52:31,126
added to you many more such things.

664
00:52:31,506 --> 00:52:36,766
Why have you despised the LORD’s word, to
do that which is evil in his sight?

665
00:52:37,466 --> 00:52:43,026
You have struck Uriah the Hittite with the
sword, have taken his wife to be your wife,

666
00:52:43,666 --> 00:52:47,526
and have slain him with the sword of the
children of Ammon.

667
00:52:47,566 --> 00:52:53,006
Now therefore the sword will never depart
from your house, because you have despised

668
00:52:53,046 --> 00:52:57,206
me and have taken Uriah the Hittite’s wife
to be your wife.’

669
00:52:57,746 --> 00:53:03,886
“This is what the LORD says: ‘Behold, I will
raise up evil against you out of your own

670
00:53:03,926 --> 00:53:10,066
house; and I will take your wives before
your eyes and give them to your neighbour, and

671
00:53:10,106 --> 00:53:13,566
he will lie with your wives in the sight
of this sun.

672
00:53:13,606 --> 00:53:19,806
For you did this secretly, but I will
do this thing before all Israel, and before the

673
00:53:19,846 --> 00:53:24,086
sun.’” David said to Nathan, “I have
sinned against the LORD.”

674
00:53:25,186 --> 00:53:29,666
Nathan said to David, “The LORD also has
put away your sin.

675
00:53:30,246 --> 00:53:31,186
You will not die.

676
00:53:31,866 --> 00:53:37,286
However, because by this deed you have
given great occasion to the LORD’s enemies to

677
00:53:37,326 --> 00:53:42,346
blaspheme, the child also who is born to
you will surely die.”

678
00:53:43,226 --> 00:53:45,566
Then Nathan departed to his house.

679
00:53:46,046 --> 00:53:51,626
The LORD struck the child that Uriah’s
wife bore to David, and he was very sick.

680
00:53:52,286 --> 00:53:58,846
David therefore begged God for the child;
and David fasted, and went in and lay all

681
00:53:58,886 --> 00:53:59,806
night on the ground.

682
00:54:00,886 --> 00:54:06,626
The elders of his house arose beside him, to
raise him up from the earth; but he would

683
00:54:06,666 --> 00:54:09,186
not, and he didn’t eat bread with them.

684
00:54:09,846 --> 00:54:12,826
On the seventh day, the child died.

685
00:54:13,366 --> 00:54:19,406
David’s servants were afraid to tell him that
the child was dead, for they said, “Behold,

686
00:54:20,046 --> 00:54:25,286
while the child was yet alive, we spoke to
him and he didn’t listen to our voice.

687
00:54:26,306 --> 00:54:30,426
How will he then harm himself if we tell
him that the child is dead?”

688
00:54:30,782 --> 00:54:36,962
But when David saw that his servants
were whispering together, David perceived that the

689
00:54:37,002 --> 00:54:42,982
child was dead; and David said to his
servants, “Is the child dead?”

690
00:54:43,642 --> 00:54:45,742
They said, “He is dead.”

691
00:54:46,902 --> 00:54:53,162
Then David arose from the earth, and
washed and anointed himself, and changed his clothing;

692
00:54:53,862 --> 00:54:57,202
and he came into the LORD’s house, and
worshipped.

693
00:54:57,242 --> 00:55:03,562
Then he came to his own house; and when
he requested, they set bread before him and he

694
00:55:03,602 --> 00:55:04,502
ate.

695
00:55:04,782 --> 00:55:08,962
Then his servants said to him, “What is
this that you have done?

696
00:55:09,662 --> 00:55:15,822
You fasted and wept for the child while he
was alive, but when the child was dead, you

697
00:55:15,862 --> 00:55:17,382
rose up and ate bread.”

698
00:55:18,202 --> 00:55:24,902
He said, “While the child was yet alive, I
fasted and wept; for I said, ‘Who

699
00:55:24,942 --> 00:55:29,642
knows whether the LORD will not be
gracious to me, that the child may live?’

700
00:55:30,422 --> 00:55:31,722
But now he is dead.

701
00:55:32,482 --> 00:55:33,382
Why should I fast?

702
00:55:34,302 --> 00:55:35,702
Can I bring him back again?

703
00:55:36,582 --> 00:55:40,062
I will go to him, but he will not return
to me.”

704
00:55:41,102 --> 00:55:46,542
David comforted Bathsheba his wife, and
went in to her, and lay with her.

705
00:55:47,422 --> 00:55:50,462
She bore a son, and he called his name
Solomon.

706
00:55:51,402 --> 00:55:58,362
The LORD loved him; and he sent by the
hand of Nathan the prophet, and he named him Jedidiah,

707
00:55:58,402 --> 00:55:59,302
for the LORD’s sake.

708
00:56:00,502 --> 00:56:05,862
Now Joab fought against Rabbah of the
children of Ammon, and took the royal city.

709
00:56:06,782 --> 00:56:12,602
Joab sent messengers to David, and said,
“I have fought against Rabbah.

710
00:56:12,642 --> 00:56:15,142
Yes, I have taken the city of waters.

711
00:56:15,862 --> 00:56:21,422
Now therefore gather the rest of the
people together, and encamp against the city and

712
00:56:21,462 --> 00:56:26,362
take it; lest I take the city, and it be
called by my name.”

713
00:56:27,562 --> 00:56:33,122
David gathered all the people together and
went to Rabbah, and fought against it and

714
00:56:33,162 --> 00:56:34,062
took it.

715
00:56:34,462 --> 00:56:39,882
He took the crown of their king from off
his head; and its weight was a talent of gold,

716
00:56:40,642 --> 00:56:45,042
and in it were precious stones; and it was
set on David’s head.

717
00:56:45,682 --> 00:56:49,302
He brought a great quantity of plunder out
of the city.

718
00:56:49,570 --> 00:56:55,410
He brought out the people who were in it,
and put them to work under saws, under iron

719
00:56:55,450 --> 00:57:02,090
picks, under axes of iron, and made them
go to the brick kiln; and he did so

720
00:57:02,130 --> 00:57:04,710
to all the cities of the children of
Ammon.

721
00:57:05,530 --> 00:57:08,910
Then David and all the people returned to
Jerusalem.

722
00:57:08,950 --> 00:57:12,490
Second Samuel, chapter thirteen.

723
00:57:12,530 --> 00:57:19,490
After this, Absalom the son of David had
a beautiful sister, whose name was Tamar; and

724
00:57:19,530 --> 00:57:21,750
Amnon the son of David loved her.

725
00:57:22,690 --> 00:57:28,810
Amnon was so troubled that he became sick
because of his sister Tamar, for she was a

726
00:57:28,850 --> 00:57:32,910
virgin, and it seemed hard to Amnon to do
anything to her.

727
00:57:33,510 --> 00:57:40,170
But Amnon had a friend whose name was
Jonadab the son of Shimeah, David’s brother; and

728
00:57:40,210 --> 00:57:42,330
Jonadab was a very subtle man.

729
00:57:42,990 --> 00:57:48,570
He said to him, “Why, son of the king, are
you so sad from day to day?

730
00:57:49,190 --> 00:57:50,130
Won’t you tell me?”

731
00:57:50,510 --> 00:57:55,310
Amnon said to him, “I love Tamar, my
brother Absalom’s sister.”

732
00:57:55,350 --> 00:58:00,610
Jonadab said to him, “Lay down on your bed
and pretend to be sick.

733
00:58:01,490 --> 00:58:07,810
When your father comes to see you, tell
him, ‘Please let my sister Tamar come and give

734
00:58:07,850 --> 00:58:13,870
me bread to eat, and prepare the food in my
sight, that I may see it and eat it from

735
00:58:13,910 --> 00:58:18,170
her hand.’” So Amnon lay down and faked
being sick.

736
00:58:19,090 --> 00:58:25,630
When the king came to see him, Amnon said
to the king, “Please let my sister Tamar come

737
00:58:25,670 --> 00:58:30,370
and make me a couple of cakes in my sight,
that I may eat from her hand.”

738
00:58:30,950 --> 00:58:38,070
Then David sent home to Tamar, saying, “Go
now to your brother Amnon’s house, and

739
00:58:38,110 --> 00:58:39,350
prepare food for him.”

740
00:58:40,230 --> 00:58:44,870
So Tamar went to her brother Amnon’s
house; and he was lying down.

741
00:58:45,850 --> 00:58:51,130
She took dough, kneaded it, made cakes in
his sight, and baked the cakes.

742
00:58:51,850 --> 00:58:56,410
She took the pan and poured them out
before him, but he refused to eat.

743
00:58:57,350 --> 00:59:00,410
Amnon said, “Have all men leave me.”

744
00:59:01,310 --> 00:59:03,330
Then every man went out from him.

745
00:59:04,230 --> 00:59:09,950
Amnon said to Tamar, “Bring the food into
the room, that I may eat from your hand.”

746
00:59:10,590 --> 00:59:16,190
Tamar took the cakes which she had made,
and brought them into the room to Amnon her

747
00:59:16,230 --> 00:59:16,882
brother.

748
00:59:16,922 --> 00:59:23,322
When she had brought them near to him to eat,
he took hold of her and said to her, “Come,

749
00:59:23,862 --> 00:59:25,262
lie with me, my sister!”

750
00:59:26,402 --> 00:59:31,122
She answered him, “No, my brother, do not
force me!

751
00:59:32,042 --> 00:59:34,322
For no such thing ought to be done in
Israel.

752
00:59:35,282 --> 00:59:36,702
Don’t you do this folly!

753
00:59:37,842 --> 00:59:40,402
As for me, where would I carry my shame?

754
00:59:41,082 --> 00:59:44,982
And as for you, you will be as one of the
fools in Israel.

755
00:59:46,022 --> 00:59:51,942
Now therefore, please speak to the king;
for he will not withhold me from you.”

756
00:59:52,342 --> 00:59:58,742
However, he would not listen to her voice;
but being stronger than she, he forced her

757
00:59:58,782 --> 01:00:00,022
and lay with her.

758
01:00:01,062 --> 01:00:06,722
Then Amnon hated her with exceedingly great
hatred; for the hatred with which he hated

759
01:00:06,762 --> 01:00:10,002
her was greater than the love with which
he had loved her.

760
01:00:11,362 --> 01:00:14,642
Amnon said to her, “Arise, be gone!”

761
01:00:15,662 --> 01:00:22,382
She said to him, “Not so, because this
great wrong in sending me away is worse than

762
01:00:22,422 --> 01:00:23,902
the other that you did to me!”

763
01:00:24,662 --> 01:00:26,422
But he would not listen to her.

764
01:00:27,102 --> 01:00:33,162
Then he called his servant who ministered to
him, and said, “Now put this woman out from

765
01:00:33,202 --> 01:00:35,642
me, and bolt the door after her.”

766
01:00:36,542 --> 01:00:41,882
She had a garment of various colours on
her, for the king’s daughters who were virgins

767
01:00:41,922 --> 01:00:43,222
dressed in such robes.

768
01:00:44,182 --> 01:00:47,722
Then his servant brought her out and
bolted the door after her.

769
01:00:48,642 --> 01:00:54,142
Tamar put ashes on her head, and tore
her garment of various colours that was on her;

770
01:00:54,862 --> 01:01:00,322
and she laid her hand on her head and went
her way, crying aloud as she went.

771
01:01:01,122 --> 01:01:05,822
Absalom her brother said to her, “Has
Amnon your brother been with you?

772
01:01:06,702 --> 01:01:08,802
But now hold your peace, my sister.

773
01:01:09,602 --> 01:01:10,502
He is your brother.

774
01:01:11,302 --> 01:01:12,702
Don’t take this thing to heart.”

775
01:01:13,962 --> 01:01:17,622
So Tamar remained desolate in her brother
Absalom’s house.

776
01:01:18,102 --> 01:01:22,282
But when King David heard of all these
things, he was very angry.

777
01:01:22,982 --> 01:01:29,682
Absalom spoke to Amnon neither good nor
bad; for Absalom hated Amnon, because

778
01:01:29,722 --> 01:01:31,762
he had forced his sister Tamar.

779
01:01:32,882 --> 01:01:39,622
After two full years, Absalom had sheep
shearers in Baal Hazor, which is beside

780
01:01:39,662 --> 01:01:43,722
Ephraim; and Absalom invited all the
king’s sons.

781
01:01:44,202 --> 01:01:50,402
Absalom came to the king and said, “See
now, your servant has sheep shearers.

782
01:01:51,322 --> 01:01:54,522
Please let the king and his servants go
with your servant.”

783
01:01:55,422 --> 01:02:02,402
The king said to Absalom, “No, my son,
let’s not all go, lest we be burdensome

784
01:02:02,442 --> 01:02:03,242
to you.”

785
01:02:03,282 --> 01:02:07,562
He pressed him; however he would not go,
but blessed him.

786
01:02:08,262 --> 01:02:13,482
Then Absalom said, “If not, please let my
brother Amnon go with us.”

787
01:02:14,202 --> 01:02:17,422
The king said to him, “Why should he go
with you?”

788
01:02:18,222 --> 01:02:23,842
But Absalom pressed him, and he let Amnon
and all the king’s sons go with him.

789
01:02:24,482 --> 01:02:31,222
Absalom commanded his servants, saying, “Mark now,
when Amnon’s heart is merry with wine;

790
01:02:32,262 --> 01:02:35,822
and when I tell you, ‘Strike Amnon,’ then
kill him.

791
01:02:36,582 --> 01:02:37,482
Don’t be afraid.

792
01:02:37,942 --> 01:02:39,222
Haven’t I commanded you?

793
01:02:39,982 --> 01:02:41,882
Be courageous, and be valiant!”

794
01:02:42,422 --> 01:02:46,422
The servants of Absalom did to Amnon as
Absalom had commanded.

795
01:02:47,342 --> 01:02:52,522
Then all the king’s sons arose, and every
man got up on his mule and fled.

796
01:02:53,522 --> 01:03:00,002
While they were on the way, the news
came to David, saying, “Absalom has slain all the

797
01:03:00,042 --> 01:03:03,182
king’s sons, and there is not one of them
left!”

798
01:03:03,762 --> 01:03:09,482
Then the king arose, and tore his garments,
and lay on the earth; and all his servants

799
01:03:09,522 --> 01:03:11,902
stood by with their clothes torn.

800
01:03:11,942 --> 01:03:18,682
Jonadab the son of Shimeah, David’s
brother, answered, “Don’t let my lord

801
01:03:18,722 --> 01:03:25,382
suppose that they have killed all the young
men, the king’s sons, for Amnon only is dead;

802
01:03:26,022 --> 01:03:30,922
for by the appointment of Absalom this has
been determined from the day that he forced

803
01:03:30,962 --> 01:03:32,222
his sister Tamar.

804
01:03:32,982 --> 01:03:39,042
Now therefore don’t let my lord the king take
the thing to his heart, to think that all

805
01:03:39,082 --> 01:03:42,822
the king’s sons are dead; for only Amnon
is dead.”

806
01:03:43,702 --> 01:03:44,802
But Absalom fled.

807
01:03:45,602 --> 01:03:51,682
The young man who kept the watch lifted
up his eyes and looked, and behold, many people

808
01:03:51,722 --> 01:03:54,462
were coming by way of the hillside behind
him.

809
01:03:54,502 --> 01:04:00,182
Jonadab said to the king, “Behold, the
king’s sons are coming!

810
01:04:00,882 --> 01:04:02,362
It is as your servant said.”

811
01:04:02,922 --> 01:04:09,442
As soon as he had finished speaking,
behold, the king’s sons came, and lifted up

812
01:04:09,482 --> 01:04:10,902
their voices and wept.

813
01:04:11,722 --> 01:04:15,122
The king also and all his servants wept
bitterly.

814
01:04:15,528 --> 01:04:22,148
But Absalom fled and went to Talmai the
son of Ammihur, king of Geshur.

815
01:04:22,188 --> 01:04:24,588
David mourned for his son every day.

816
01:04:25,668 --> 01:04:30,428
So Absalom fled and went to Geshur, and
was there three years.

817
01:04:30,928 --> 01:04:37,188
King David longed to go out to
Absalom, for he was comforted concerning Amnon, since

818
01:04:37,228 --> 01:04:37,888
he was dead.

819
01:04:37,928 --> 01:04:41,788
Second Samuel, chapter fourteen.

820
01:04:41,828 --> 01:04:47,788
Now Joab the son of Zeruiah perceived that
the king’s heart was towards Absalom.

821
01:04:48,908 --> 01:04:55,568
Joab sent to Tekoa and brought a wise
woman from there, and said to her, “Please act

822
01:04:55,608 --> 01:05:00,928
like a mourner, and put on mourning
clothing, please, and don’t anoint yourself with

823
01:05:00,968 --> 01:05:05,388
oil; but be as a woman who has mourned a
long time for the dead.

824
01:05:06,228 --> 01:05:09,428
Go in to the king and speak like this to
him.”

825
01:05:10,288 --> 01:05:12,568
So Joab put the words in her mouth.

826
01:05:12,608 --> 01:05:18,588
When the woman of Tekoa spoke to the king,
she fell on her face to the ground, showed

827
01:05:18,628 --> 01:05:21,648
respect, and said, “Help, O king!”

828
01:05:22,268 --> 01:05:24,908
The king said to her, “What ails you?”

829
01:05:25,748 --> 01:05:30,328
She answered, “Truly I am a widow, and my
husband is dead.

830
01:05:31,368 --> 01:05:36,728
Your servant had two sons; and they both
fought together in the field, and there was

831
01:05:36,768 --> 01:05:41,148
no one to part them, but the one struck
the other and killed him.

832
01:05:41,648 --> 01:05:48,228
Behold, the whole family has risen against
your servant, and they say, ‘Deliver him who

833
01:05:48,268 --> 01:05:53,148
struck his brother, that we may kill him
for the life of his brother whom he killed,

834
01:05:53,888 --> 01:05:55,768
